# Draft §7, consequence 1: `flow` and `rank` are NOT keywords of
# this genre, and their absence is a CONSEQUENCE rather than a refusal ruling
# of its own — which is why they get the plain allowlist message and not one of
# the three named refusal diagnostics.
#
# The reason: both of this genre's axes are already ordered by the source.
# Columns are in `lifeline` declaration order and time runs down the page in
# the order the occurrence lines are written, so a key that reordered either
# would make the drawing disagree with the text (`DECLARATION-ORDER-SEMANTICS`). There is nothing for
# them to set.
figdown 0.4 sequence
lifeline c "C"
lifeline s "S"
flow down
rank c,s
